# Copy to `.env` and adjust, then rebuild (`npm run tauri dev` / `tauri ios
# dev`). Vite reads these at build time — changing `.env` requires a rebuild,
# it won't hot-reload. Both are optional: with neither set, the app defaults
# to a relay on the same machine (127.0.0.1:8765).
#
# On desktop you can also override the profile list at runtime from the
# app's DevTools console (see README) — useful for switching relays without
# rebuilding. iOS has no DevTools access, so these build-time env vars are
# the only way to point an iOS build at a relay.

# Host/IP of the machine running the relay.
# VITE_ULTRON_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Port the relay listens on (RELAY_PORT in relay/.env.example).
# VITE_ULTRON_PORT=8765
